&nbsp;

  &nbsp;

What you’ll do &nbsp;

The Design Director leads creative direction and design strategy across key client projects. Combining deep brand expertise with a strong understanding of client businesses and audiences, they develop compelling, integrated design solutions that meet client needs, strengthen brands and support business growth.

Key Responsibilities

• Set and lead design direction across multiple projects, from concept through production.

• Develop innovative ideas across digital, print and experiential channels, grounded in audience insight and the client brief.

• Partner with clients, production teams, Client Services and other discipline leads to deliver high-quality work on time and to agreed financial targets.

• Act as creative lead on client projects and pitches when required, and build strong client relationships.

• Champion design excellence by sharing a clear point of view, critiquing work and helping teams elevate their creative output.

• Hire, onboard, mentor and inspire talent, fostering a positive, empowering culture where people are supported and challenged.

• Identify opportunities to strengthen the team, improve its capabilities and support future growth.

• Collaborate across teams to maintain design consistency and solve complex strategic and creative challenges.

  &nbsp;

What you’ll need &nbsp;

&nbsp;

• Significant design experience in a brand-focused creative agency or similar environment.

• A strong strategic and creative point of view, with the ability to turn bold ideas into distinctive, high-quality design.

• Excellent conceptual skills and a track record of developing innovative brand-led work.

• A sophisticated understanding of visual identity and how to bring brand elements-such as messaging, colour, imagery and typography-to life across deliverables.

• Confidence presenting design strategies and telling compelling stories to clients, stakeholders and teams.

• Strong communication and relationship-building skills, with the business acumen to manage stakeholders, grow client relationships and identify commercial opportunities.

• Financial awareness, including the ability to set and work towards financial goals for projects and teams.

• Proven ability to lead, motivate and encourage project teams with an optimistic, growth-oriented approach.

• A strong awareness of design and creative trends, as well as the cultural, industry and global shifts influencing how people engage with brands.

• A passion for design, branding and creative excellence.

• Proficiency with creative tools such as Adobe Creative Suite, Figma, Miro and AI tools, alongside traditional techniques like hand sketching.

